premise, of course, and edge.

00:09:29.050 --> 00:09:33.790
And second, that Anthos
is exactly this stack,

00:09:33.790 --> 00:09:37.450
and that it will play a
role similar to what Linux

00:09:37.450 --> 00:09:42.700
played 20 years or so ago.

00:09:42.700 --> 00:09:49.230
So Anthos is as safe and as
clear a choice as back then

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:53.590
was choosing Linux, because
it runs everywhere, it's based

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.715
on open source and Kubernetes.

00:09:56.715 --> 00:09:58.090
Because it's based
on Kubernetes,

00:09:58.090 --> 00:10:00.670
everything will
run on top of that.

00:10:00.670 --> 00:10:03.550
And so that makes an
Anthos a safe choice

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:06.560
for the next decade or two,
because when you choose it,

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:10.210
you don't really give up
any other choices, just

00:10:10.210 --> 00:10:11.830
like when you choose Linux.

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:15.640
So that, in a nutshell, was what
